# openclaw is DELIBERATELY NOT in this list (removed 2026-08-27).
#
# History (beta era; full evidence chain:
# ~/repos/hart/docs/openclaw-beta-drift-check.md): `openclaw@latest` here was
# the root cause of four silent beta->stable downgrades (2026-08-17 x2,
# 2026-08-22 16:26, 2026-08-26 02:02 +1000) -- each landed 2-3 min after a
# fast-forward `git pull` here (post-merge -> deploy.zsh ->
# scripts/deploy.d/70_runtime_installs.zsh npm sweep), and the stable binary
# refused the beta-written config (exit 78), bricking the CLI/gateway.
#
# Since 2026-09-02 ceres runs the STABLE channel (openclaw 2026.8.2,
# update.channel: "stable" in ~/repos/hart/openclaw/openclaw.json). openclaw
# stays out of this list regardless of channel: any deploy reinstalls it
# *under the live gateway*, rewriting dist/ beneath a running process and
# breaking its lazy module loading until restart. Ownership stays with the
# two paths that cannot fire mid-run:
#   - upgrades: openclaw's own in-gateway auto-updater (stable-tracking)
#   - repair/install: ~/repos/hart/scripts/openclaw-ensure-stable.sh, the
#     ExecStartPre guard on openclaw-gateway.service (self-heals a missing
#     package on node bumps too)
# tsc/tsserver + the LSP server nvim's ts_ls uses.
